{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-81743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following vector fields are conservative on ${R}^{2}?$\n\n- $F=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\,i+y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\,j$\n- $G=(2x+1)\\,i+(5{y}^{2}+2y+1)\\,j$\n- $H={y}^{2}\\,i+{x}^{2}\\,j$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-81743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $F(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j$ be a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first-order partial derivatives everywhere on $D.$ Then, we have the following theorem:\n\n$F$ *is conservative if and only if $\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}$ everywhere on $D.$*\n\nNote that for each of our functions, $D={R}^{2}.$ With this in mind, let's check each of the vector fields. \n\n- For the vector field $F,$ we have $P=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)$ and $Q=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy).$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy),\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are not equal, we conclude that $F$ is not conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $G,$ we have $P=2x+1$ and $Q=5{y}^{2}+2y+1.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $G$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $H,$ we have $P={y}^{2}$ and $Q={x}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are not equal, we conclude that $H$ is not conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-81743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b13b02c6380fe5a8c9febc03ece01dee022a65148c2d353d623df7d6600d1659"} {"question" "q-81743" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-81743" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-81743" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-81746" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following vector fields are conservative on ${R}^{2}?$\n\n- $F=xy\\,i+(\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,j$\n- $G=(4x+{y}^{2})\\,i-4x{y}^{2}\\,j$\n- $H=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\,j$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-81746" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $F(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j$ be a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first-order partial derivatives everywhere on $D.$ Then, we have the following theorem:\n\n$F$ *is conservative if and only if $\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}$ everywhere on $D.$*\n\nNote that for each of our functions, $D={R}^{2}.$ With this in mind, let's check each of the vector fields.  \n\n- For the vector field $F,$ we have $P=xy$ and $Q=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=x,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $F$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $G,$ we have $P=4x+{y}^{2}$ and $Q=-4x{y}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-4{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are not equal, we conclude that $G$ is not conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $H,$ we have $P=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)$ and $Q=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy).$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy),\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy),.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are not equal, we conclude that $H$ is not conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-81746" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b13b02c6380fe5a8c9febc03ece01dee022a65148c2d353d623df7d6600d1659"} {"question" "q-81746" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-81746" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-81746" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-104573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following vector fields are conservative on ${R}^{2}?$\n\n- $F=(2x-y)\\,i-x\\,j$\n- $G=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\,i+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\,j$\n- $H={e}^{x-y}\\,i-{e}^{x-y}\\,j$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-104573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $F(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j$ be a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first-order partial derivatives everywhere on $D.$ Then, we have the following theorem:\n\n$F$ *is conservative if and only if $\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}$ everywhere on $D.$*\n\nNote that for each of our functions, $D={R}^{2}.$ With this in mind, let's check each of the vector fields. \n\n- For the vector field $F,$ we have $P=2x-y$ and $Q=-x.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-1.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $F$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $G,$ we have $P=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$ and $Q=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy).$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy),\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy).\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $G$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $H,$ we have $P={e}^{x-y}$ and $Q=-{e}^{x-y}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-{e}^{x-y},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-{e}^{x-y}.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on ${R}^{2},$ we conclude that $H$ is conservative on ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-104573" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b13b02c6380fe5a8c9febc03ece01dee022a65148c2d353d623df7d6600d1659"} {"question" "q-104573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-104573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-104573" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-123993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector field $F=({y}^{3}-ay)\\,i+(3x{y}^{2}-2x)\\,j$ on ${R}^{2}$, where $a$ is a constant. Given that $F$ is conservative, find the value of $a.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-123993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $F(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j$ be a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first-order partial derivatives everywhere on $D.$ Then, we have the following theorem:\n\n$F$ *is conservative if and only if $\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}$ everywhere on $D.$*\n\nFor the vector field $F,$ the domain $D={R}^{2},$ and we have \n\n$$\nP={y}^{3}-ay,\\,Q=3x{y}^{2}-2x.\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=3{y}^{2}-a,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=3{y}^{2}-2.\n$$\n\nIt's clear that the partial derivatives exist and are continuous on ${R}^{2}.$ Equating the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}-a & =3{y}^{2}-2 \\\\ -a & =-2 \\\\ a & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $a=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-123993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b13b02c6380fe5a8c9febc03ece01dee022a65148c2d353d623df7d6600d1659"} {"question" "q-123993" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-123993" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-123993" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-124000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vector field $F=(ax{y}^{2}+1)\\,i+(4{x}^{2}y+1)\\,j$ on ${R}^{2}$, where $a$ is a constant. Given that $F$ is conservative, find the value of $a.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-124000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $F(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j$ be a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first-order partial derivatives everywhere on $D.$ Then, we have the following theorem:\n\n$F$ *is conservative if and only if $\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}$ everywhere on $D.$*\n\nFor the vector field $F,$ the domain $D={R}^{2},$ and we have \n\n$$\nP=ax{y}^{2}+1,\\,Q=4{x}^{2}y+1.\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2axy,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=8xy.\n$$\n\nIt's clear that the partial derivatives exist and are continuous on ${R}^{2}.$ Equating the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2axy & =8xy \\\\ 2axy-8xy & =0 \\\\ 2(a-4)xy & =0 \\\\ a-4 & =0 \\\\ a & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the last equality must be satisfied everywhere on $D,$ we conclude that $a-4=0,$ that is, $a=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-124000" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b13b02c6380fe5a8c9febc03ece01dee022a65148c2d353d623df7d6600d1659"} {"question" "q-124000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-124000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"} {"question" "q-124000" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066733/state.json" "file_sha256" "b2403d754f7163775d435b94a8f24db1eaa3576603106ed10c276acadb9df19b"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2202 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
